{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq90djykq63","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: diagnostics / any new field added to overlay naively only persists in ephemeral JSON — survives save() but NOT a JSON wipe","summary":"When adding a new field (e.g. diagnostics, metrics, timestamps) to overlay.js, the naive approach adds it to EMPTY() and LOCAL_FIELDS. This stores the data in the overlay JSON file, which is treated as ephemeral and may be wiped/regenerated. After a JSON wipe, load() returns null for the field even though data was set. The durable path: (1) emit a graph-store event via emitDiff() — add a case in the emitDiff loop that calls graphStore.appendEvent(store, id, {evt:\"diagnostics_set\", ...}); (2) handle the event in graph-store.js switch to reconstruct node.diagnostics; (3) rehydrate in overlay.js load() from the graph-store node. Do NOT add the field to LOCAL_FIELDS — that makes it ephemeral. Discovered when diagnostics field failed to survive overlay JSON deletion in bench grader. Fields correctly routed through graph-store: assignee, timestamps, metrics, measurements.","created_by":"bench-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T04:39:38.828Z","vec":[-0.06402471661567688,0.09341567754745483,0.020501064136624336,0.08333272486925125,0.0695294588804245,-0.07432181388139725,-0.0706229880452156,0.013344458304345608,0.01068634632974863,0.04006161913275719,0.07984083890914917,0.014029266312718391,-0.054683342576026917,-0.009332791902124882,0.040576670318841934,0.02054128237068653,0.00778990238904953,-0.06133697181940079,-0.07777978479862213,-0.018547696992754936,-0.05148490145802498,-0.03940543159842491,-0.015191122889518738,0.034575581550598145,0.035376645624637604,0.02539793774485588,-0.06224667653441429,-0.0012378209503367543,0.011025598272681236,-0.00007572123286081478,-0.000817401974927634,0.01985527202486992,-0.0313602015376091,0.03936736285686493,0.005932413972914219,0.07851790636777878,0.00007164368435041979,0.02128732204437256,-0.001835868